From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ioupsd: declare needsMerge, which the drop never sets

upsd.m tests needsMerge before initializing a battery case's AC state,
but nothing in the published PowerManagement source declares or sets it.
Stock /usr/libexec/ioupsd (macOS 26.5.2, 25F84) shows the missing code:
it reads the device's "Transport Type" and, for "Inductive In-Band",
reuses an already-registered battery case record from a global with the
flag set; every other device goes through GetPrivateData() with it
clear.  Declare it false, which is what stock does for all but inductive
in-band battery cases; merging those is left undone.

--- a/ioupsd/upsd.m	2026-09-15 12:14:58
+++ b/ioupsd/upsd.m	2026-09-15 12:14:58
@@ -464,6 +464,7 @@
     IOCFPlugInInterface **  plugInInterface 	= NULL;
     IOUPSPlugInInterface_v140 ** upsPlugInInterface = NULL;
     HRESULT                 result              = S_FALSE;
+    bool                    needsMerge          = false;
     IOReturn                kr;
     SInt32                  score;
 
